    "authoredFrom": "Read from the case's input bytes: grund.toml (version 1, `strict = false`, default scan and `[id] format`, and two configured kinds with no title: FS in docs/functional-spec, indexed by its README, and E2E in e2e/cases with `index = false`). E2E is a configured kind, not a default (§FS-config.3.4.4.3), so the case machinery follows its home (§FS-declarations.e2e-case). e2e/cases/001-inner-fixture sits directly in that folder, holds expected.exit and its name reads as an E2E ID under `{kind}-{number}-{slug}`, so it declares E2E-001-inner-fixture (§FS-declarations.e2e-case.id), located at the directory, line 1, with no sections and no title (§FS-list.3.2); its manifest has no command.args, so its args are empty and its invocation `grund check`, its expected exit the `1` of its expected.exit, and its fixtures the four files under it, relative and sorted (§FS-show.2.4, §FS-show.2.4.2, §AR-scanner.6.2); nothing cites it and a case is never unused (§FS-check.4.1.3). The walk does not enter the case directory, so its nested fixture repository, with its FS-001-inner and that file's dangling FS-999-missing, is no content of this project (§FS-declarations.e2e-case.walk, §AR-scanner.6.4): it declares and cites nothing and draws no finding. FS-001-alpha (body line 3) cites FS-002-beta and FS-002-beta (body line 3) cites FS-001-alpha, both marked, and the FS index lists both by full links with their anchors, so every outer declaration is used and listed, and the one finding is the site-less version caution (§FS-check.2.1.1). Cross-reference emission wraps each body's marked citation as a link to the other file's heading anchor (§FS-fmt.6.2, §FS-fmt.6.2.1) and leaves the index entries, already canonical, as written (§FS-fmt.6.3). The golden pins check: exit 0, an empty stdout and the version caution on stderr. FS-404 is the absent control.",
